# Last Updated Date Rule

Whenever you make a **material** change to an existing page's substantive content, update that page's last-updated metadata to the **actual modification date** (today's real calendar date, ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` or matching human format used by that content type).

## Where to store the date

| Page type | Field / location |
|-----------|------------------|
| Research (`src/content/blog/`) | Frontmatter `updatedDate` (keep `date` as original publish date) |
| News (`src/data/newsArticles.ts`) | `dateModified` (ISO); keep `datePublished` / `date` |
| Pathway landings | Per-entry `lastReviewed` in `src/lib/pathwayRoutes.ts` (do **not** change the shared default for unrelated pages) |
| Tools, About, Process, Playbook, Resources, FAQ detail, PCS | Override the path in `src/lib/pageFreshness.ts` → `pageLastUpdated` |

Display uses `src/components/LastUpdated.astro`. Article JSON-LD `dateModified` must match the same value (ISO via `toIsoDate()`).

## Material updates (DO bump the date)

- Factual, legal, immigration, investment, or regulatory changes
- Stats, dollar amounts, deadlines, timelines, eligibility, pricing
- New or substantially rewritten sections
- Correcting outdated information
- Meaningful new research content

## Non-material updates (DO NOT bump the date)

- Typos, formatting-only, CSS/spacing/color tweaks
- Refactors with no content change
- Nav/footer/layout chrome that does not change page substance
- Link URL fixes that do not change meaning
- Build/deploy/config-only changes

## Hard prohibitions

- Never set last-updated from build time, deploy time, or "today" on every page
- Never mass-refresh dates across the site to fake freshness
- Never replace a legitimate `date` / `datePublished` with the modification date
- Do not add last-updated UI to excluded utilities: contact, privacy, 404, homepage, listing hubs (research/faq/news/pathways/tools indexes), form-only pages
